[
    {
        "content": "<p>I've been working on a PR for Hall's Theorems, and I have a few generally useful lemmas I've needed. Wanted to see if any of these are in mathlib in a different form or if they are/aren't warranted additions.</p>\n<p>Sup of characteristic subgroups is characteristic.:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iSup_characteristic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Sort</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ι</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Subgroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Characteristic</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⨆</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Characteristic</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Cardinality for <code>noncommPiCoprod</code></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">card_iSup_of_iSupIndep</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hcomm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Pairwise</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Commute</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hind</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">iSupIndep</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">⨆</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∏</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">card</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">H</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(Also, <code>card_biSup_of_iSupIndep</code> for Finsets?)</p>\n<p>\"the last nontrivial derived subgroup is abelian\"</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">derivedSeries_succ_eq_bot_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"n\">derivedSeries</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊥</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsMulCommutative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">derivedSeries</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>We have <code>commutator_eq_bot_iff</code>, but inducting on derived length needs the statement for a general derived term, not just the whole group.</p>",
        "id": 600714666,
        "sender_full_name": "Richard Osborn",
        "timestamp": 1780674572
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Certainly that first one looks reasonable, and we should have the <code>sSup</code> and <code>sup</code> versions too.</p>",
        "id": 600729390,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780679182
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For the second one I wonder if we have a better way to spell <code>hcomm</code>; though I'd also expect the proof to go via constructing the isomoprhism, so that it works for <code>Cardinal.mk</code> too</p>",
        "id": 600730114,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1780679474
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The only snag with using the isomorphism for <code>Cardinal.mk</code> is that <code>#(⨆ i, H i)</code> and <code>#(∀ i, H i)</code> are in different universes. I'm not sure the desired way to resolve that.</p>",
        "id": 600746258,
        "sender_full_name": "Richard Osborn",
        "timestamp": 1780684956
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>you can lift them both to the same universe, see also <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39807\">#39807</a></p>",
        "id": 600747940,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1780685634
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"560559\">Richard Osborn</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Additional.20Group.20Theory.20Lemmas/near/600714666\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>\"the last nontrivial derived subgroup is abelian\"</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">derivedSeries_succ_eq_bot_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">     </span><span class=\"n\">derivedSeries</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊥</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsMulCommutative</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">derivedSeries</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>We have <code>commutator_eq_bot_iff</code>, but inducting on derived length needs the statement for a general derived term, not just the whole group.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/39956\">#39956</a> has <code>commutator_self_eq_bot : ⁅H, H⁆ = ⊥ ↔ IsMulCommutative H</code> if it helps</p>",
        "id": 600802671,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1780710390
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"310045\">Eric Wieser</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/217875-Is-there-code-for-X.3F/topic/Additional.20Group.20Theory.20Lemmas/near/600729390\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Certainly that first one looks reasonable, and we should have the <code>sSup</code> and <code>sup</code> versions too.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>and biSup, to match <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Subgroup.sup_normal#doc\">docs#Subgroup.sup_normal</a> / <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Subgroup.iSup_normal#doc\">docs#Subgroup.iSup_normal</a> / <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Subgroup.biSup_normal#doc\">docs#Subgroup.biSup_normal</a> / <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=Subgroup.sSup_normal#doc\">docs#Subgroup.sSup_normal</a></p>",
        "id": 600802884,
